WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.090
Robert Pattinson is doing a little backtracking.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.970
The star of the upcoming The Batman reversed
course on an assertion he's made a couple

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.520
of times in recent months: that Batman isn't
actually a superhero.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.120
Pattinson first put forth his Bat-opinion
during a conversation with The New York Times

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.520
in October of last year.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.600
While it's understandable that his opinion
would be a touch controversial among fans,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.830
it's also kind of tough to argue with, and
it illustrates the interesting approach the

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.360
actor seems to be taking to portraying the
character.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:27.880
He said:

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.480
"Batman's not a hero...he's a complicated
character.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.280
I don't think I could ever play a real hero,
there's always got to be something a little

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.980
bit wrong...[Batman's] morality is a little
bit off.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.240
He's not the golden boy, unlike almost every
other comic-book character.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.430
There is a simplicity to his worldview, but
where it sits is strange, which allows you

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.060
to have more scope with the character."

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.420
Okay, that's all well and good, but Pattinson
really ran into trouble in December, during

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.579
a sit down with Today.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.420
At that time, the star doubled down in a big
way:

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.940
"Batman is not a superhero.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.720
It's weird.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.730
I always balk at it.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:01.730
It doesn't count.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.560
You need to have, like, magical powers or
something."

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.500
All we can do is speculate as to whether Pattinson
has ever heard of the many, many superheroes

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.180
who don't technically have any powers.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.640
Of course, when he finally did reverse track
on this controversial opinion, Pattinson did

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.380
so in typically cheeky fashion.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.700
Speaking with TimeOut, the actor explained
that he thought he'd lost the role when the

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:24.310
fact that he was being eyed for it by Warner
Bros. was publicly leaked.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:28.630
He was obviously excited when he was cast,
but ever since landing the coveted part, the

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.320
star has been the subject of plenty of fan
complaints.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.840
Some of them, it seems, just don't think he's
cut out for the role, and those "not a superhero"

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.100
remarks didn't do anything to win them over.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.260
Pattinson is quite aware of that fact, and
he explained to TimeOut that if he had simply

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.770
brushed up a bit more on his DC lore, he wouldn't
have said what he said.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.990
That said, he didn't exactly back all the
way off of his comments.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:49.820
According to him:

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.000
"I wasn't educated about the subject.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.740
People got very angry about it.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.680
It's bizarre.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.560
I still can't understand the argument.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.100
Okay, he's a superhero, I'm sorry!

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.320
The next headline: 'Pattinson retracts: Batman
is, in fact, a superhero.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.420
He takes it back.'"

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.860
Despite the insane level of scrutiny that
comes with being cast as the Caped Crusader,

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.700
though, Pattinson is still beyond excited
for those fans to actually see the film.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.360
He said:

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.280
"I'm only worried about [whether] people like
it when it's done.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.380
Right now, people can think what they want...It's
the coolest thing ever.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.880
I still can't really believe it."

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:25.060
We suppose his backtracking can't hurt his
standing with the fans, but many of them will

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.450
forever disparage Pattinson's casting purely
because of his involvement with the Twilight

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:29.940
saga.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.940
"That's all superhero stuff, right?

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.340
What if I'm not the hero.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.320
What if I'm the bad guy?"

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.010
We've pointed this out on several occasions
before, but since a lot of fans seem to keep

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:45.069
missing it, we're going to go ahead and do
it again: Pattinson is a far better actor

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:47.520
than his stint in the Twilight movies would
suggest.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.280
For recent evidence, look no further than
his incredible performance in The Lighthouse.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.560
If you're still not convinced, we submit 2017's
Good Time, a harrowing crime drama from the

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.520
Safdie brothers, who just turned in another
minor masterpiece with Uncut Gems.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.840
Pattinson's desperate turn as a crook trying
to scrounge up the dough to spring his simple-minded

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.220
brother from jail must be seen to be believed.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:12.260
Pattinson also delivered a stunning performance
in the 2018 sci-fi drama High Life, in which

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.620
he portrayed one of two survivors of a doomed
deep-space mission.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.240
What we're saying here is that Pattinson has
spent his entire post-Twilight career absolutely

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.600
crushing it in extremely challenging roles.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.440
That's why we're so certain that Pattinson
is a perfect choice to play Batman.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.520
Of course, the proof will be in the finished
product.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.670
The Batman is currently before the cameras,
and is slated to hit the big screen on June

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.640
25, 2021.

